WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:14.663
had a Red Share with Gliss?"

2
00:00:15.064 --> 00:00:16.244
Perda sounded surprised.

3
00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:19.065
"I didn't know you two were so close."

4
00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.886
"Me neither," Darb said quietly.

5
00:00:22.586 --> 00:00:23.726
Zann didn't say anything.

6
00:00:24.046 --> 00:00:25.186
He was surprised himself.

7
00:00:26.047 --> 00:00:30.028
Usually Red Shares only happened between family members or very close friends.

8
00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:33.578
"Gliss is the girl who was captured this morning, yes?"

9
00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:34.918
Teplo said thoughtfully.

10
00:00:34.938 --> 00:00:40.822
"It's interesting that you received the Share now rather than when the trolls grabbed her."

11
00:00:41.522 --> 00:00:42.162
Perda nodded.

12
00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:45.564
"I'm sure Gliss has been terrified ever since she was taken.

13
00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:48.866
The Share means something just scared her even more."

14
00:00:49.527 --> 00:00:50.807
Teplo yanked the rope again.

15
00:00:50.827 --> 00:00:52.628
"Where is Fala?"

16
00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:53.549
he exclaimed.

17
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.410
A door opened in the back of the room.

18
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.132
"Sorry," Fala said breathlessly.

19
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.721
"I was distracted, watching the trolls on the Remote Eye."

20
00:01:02.741 --> 00:01:04.982
"What's a Remote Eye?"

21
00:01:05.322 --> 00:01:05.943
Perda asked.

22
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:07.543
Fala glanced at her.

23
00:01:07.563 --> 00:01:10.264
"Hey, you're the kids who knocked on the door.

24
00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:11.445
How'd you get down here?"

25
00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:14.046
She shot a suspicious look at Teplo.

26
00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:16.167
"Did you use the trapdoor?

27
00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:18.848
I told you—that thing's dangerous!"

28
00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:20.989
Teplo grinned sheepishly.

29
00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:22.970
"I put cushions under the hole."

30
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.830
Fala rolled her eyes.

31
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.232
"Sorry about that," she told the kids.

32
00:01:29.308 --> 00:01:32.170
Then she noticed that Darb was gnawing on a turnip cookie.

33
00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.650
"Are you hungry?

34
00:01:34.051 --> 00:01:36.192
You don't have to eat those disgusting things."

35
00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:38.853
"Disgusting?" Teplo said.

36
00:01:38.873 --> 00:01:41.835
"Turnips are extremely nutritious!"

37
00:01:42.195 --> 00:01:45.837
Ignoring him, Fala conjured some food and a pitcher of airberry juice.

38
00:01:45.857 --> 00:01:47.578
"Thank you!"

39
00:01:48.118 --> 00:01:48.859
Perda exclaimed.

40
00:01:48.879 --> 00:01:50.980
"We can't use magic right now."

41
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.061
"I know he can't."

42
00:01:53.461 --> 00:01:54.542
Fala pointed at Zann.

43
00:01:54.562 --> 00:01:58.624
"But as far as we know, the trolls are only targeting Reds."

44
00:01:59.392 --> 00:02:01.194
"That's what I thought," Teplo said.

45
00:02:01.214 --> 00:02:03.275
"But wait until you hear their story!"

46
00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.158
He told Fala what the kids had just told him.

47
00:02:06.178 --> 00:02:09.581
"That's quite a tale," she said when he was finished.

48
00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:12.323
"I think I saw Gliss on the Remote Eye this morning.

49
00:02:13.103 --> 00:02:14.905
She's a pretty girl about your age, right?"

50
00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:18.428
Zann realized that Fala had never answered Perda's question.

51
00:02:18.448 --> 00:02:20.850
"What's a Remote Eye?"

52
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:21.751
he asked.

53
00:02:21.771 --> 00:02:27.996
"It's an ancient type of magic, long forgotten in these peaceful times," Teplo said.

54
00:02:28.724 --> 00:02:34.147
"It's a way to watch someone without being seen—and without using a spy fly."

55
00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:35.548
Fala nodded.

56
00:02:35.568 --> 00:02:42.872
"In the Old Times, Magicians often created devices that focused their energy through certain arrangements of special objects.

57
00:02:43.712 --> 00:02:48.895
Some of the plans still exist, though these ancient texts are only available to advanced scholars at the

58
00:02:48.955 --> 00:02:51.056
university." "Why?"

59
00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:52.037
Perda asked.

60
00:02:52.057 --> 00:02:56.579
"If these old devices make better magic, shouldn't everyone know about them?"

61
00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:59.404
"It's not that simple," replied Teplo.

62
00:02:59.424 --> 00:03:03.165
"The devices often had unintended side effects.

63
00:03:03.966 --> 00:03:09.727
Besides, many devices required components that are unlawful or immoral to possess today."

64
00:03:09.747 --> 00:03:11.188
"Like what?"

65
00:03:11.548 --> 00:03:12.068
said Zann.

66
00:03:13.108 --> 00:03:14.168
Teplo looked uneasy.

67
00:03:14.188 --> 00:03:20.330
"Well, for instance, a Remote Eye was originally supposed to contain an actual eye."

68
00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.531
"You mean a person's eye?"

69
00:03:22.811 --> 00:03:24.091
Darb sounded horrified.

70
00:03:24.111 --> 00:03:26.932
"Ideally, yes," Teplo said.

71
00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.183
"Though some books suggested using the eye of a dragon instead."

72
00:03:31.203 --> 00:03:33.285
"Is that what you used?"

73
00:03:33.685 --> 00:03:35.247
Zann exclaimed, thinking of Zing.

74
00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:37.248
"A dragon's eye?"

75
00:03:37.268 --> 00:03:39.390
"Of course not!"

76
00:03:39.751 --> 00:03:40.311
Fala said.

77
00:03:40.331 --> 00:03:45.075
"We've been experimenting with alternatives, and we finally found one that works.

78
00:03:45.896 --> 00:03:48.538
It's a telescope lens that I borrowed from a Void friend."

79
00:03:48.558 --> 00:03:50.540
"What's a telescope?"

80
00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.481
Perda asked.

81
00:03:52.201 --> 00:03:54.864
"It helps you see stuff that's far away," Darb told her.

82
00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.581
"It works sort of like a Sight Enhancing spell."

83
00:03:58.482 --> 00:04:03.865
"Now if only we could concoct an eardrum substitute, we might be able to hear the trolls as

84
00:04:03.925 --> 00:04:05.686
well as see them," Teplo said.

85
00:04:05.706 --> 00:04:10.229
"Meanwhile, Fala, is there any news from our contacts at the palace?"

86
00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.510
"A little."

87
00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.850
Fala looked worried.

88
00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.873
"The king's assistant just volunteered to take over as king."

89
00:04:16.893 --> 00:04:20.515
"You mean that sneaky little fellow, Slib?"

90
00:04:20.855 --> 00:04:21.976
Teplo rolled his eyes.

91
00:04:22.732 --> 00:04:26.053
"He's not fit to rule his own house, let alone Magica."

92
00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:29.814
"He claims the era of Reds is over," Fala said.

93
00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:36.216
"The Red Council—that is, what's left of it—can't do much to prevent him from grabbing power, since the

94
00:04:36.256 --> 00:04:37.476
members are all in hiding."

95
00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:40.497
"Well, I'll let the others worry about that."

96
00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:41.537
Teplo shrugged.

97
00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:43.858
"I don't care about politics.

98
00:04:44.658 --> 00:04:47.279
What I do care about is helping the trolls' prisoners."

99
00:04:48.499 --> 00:04:49.179
Zann nodded.

100
00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:51.700
"We have to figure out how to save Gliss.

101
00:04:52.548 --> 00:04:54.469
Let's go scout out that dragon pen."

102
00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.592
"Out of the question," Teplo said.

103
00:04:57.612 --> 00:04:58.912
"It's far too dangerous."

104
00:04:58.932 --> 00:05:03.035
"But she's only there because of me," Zann insisted.

105
00:05:03.055 --> 00:05:04.656
"I have to save her!"

106
00:05:05.417 --> 00:05:07.498
The others all tried to change his mind.

107
00:05:08.179 --> 00:05:11.501
But Zann was determined, arguing against whatever they said.

108
00:05:12.241 --> 00:05:13.722
Finally Teplo sighed.

109
00:05:13.742 --> 00:05:18.085
"He's just as stubborn as his grandfather," he muttered.

110
00:05:18.105 --> 00:05:19.787
"Go if you must, Zann.

111
00:05:20.147 --> 00:05:21.528
But you'll need a disguise."

112
00:05:22.376 --> 00:05:24.718
"If he's going, I'll go too," Perda said.

113
00:05:24.738 --> 00:05:26.739
"No," Teplo said.

114
00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.860
"It's safer if Zann goes alone."

115
00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.182
"He's right," Zann said.

116
00:05:31.202 --> 00:05:33.303
"You and Darb should stay here."

117
00:05:34.283 --> 00:05:35.584
Teplo glanced at Fala.

118
00:05:35.604 --> 00:05:39.387
"Please send a message to the other Reds who remain free.

119
00:05:40.207 --> 00:05:43.349
Maybe they can help keep an eye on Zann in case he gets in trouble."

120
00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:47.792
He sounded doubtful, but Fala nodded and summoned several message moths.

121
00:05:51.252 --> 00:05:53.634
Then she went to work on Zann's disguise.

122
00:05:54.875 --> 00:05:59.358
Teplo tried to convince her to turn Zann's hair purple, but she made it brown instead.

123
00:06:00.098 --> 00:06:02.680
She also hid Zann's freckles with an Illusion spell.

124
00:06:04.981 --> 00:06:07.603
The streets were deserted when Zann left Teplo's house.

125
00:06:08.264 --> 00:06:09.925
The zoo was a dozen blocks away.

126
00:06:10.345 --> 00:06:13.747
While he walked, Zann tried to come up with a plan to free Gliss.

127
00:06:14.568 --> 00:06:17.510
How could he defeat Morb's trolls without using magic?

128
00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.532
Zann was still thinking as he rounded a corner.

129
00:06:21.288 --> 00:06:23.231
Suddenly he heard a rustle of movement.

130
00:06:23.832 --> 00:06:28.479
But before he could react, he found himself trapped in a dark, floating bubble!

131
00:06:28.499 --> 00:06:30.382
"What's going on?"

132
00:06:30.782 --> 00:06:31.223
he cried.

133
00:06:31.243 --> 00:06:34.748
"We know that you're a Red," said a low voice.

134
00:06:34.768 --> 00:06:36.871
"You'll need to come with us."
